1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Previously on JoJo's Bizarre Adventure...

2
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:17,060
Blast it!

3
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:19,720
Oh no, the exit's blocked with ice!

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,720
And more is coming this way!

5
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,940
Hey, shit!

6
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,797
It's time to cover the whole tunnel!

7
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:30,900
I gotta find a way out of this death trap!

8
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,250
What?

9
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,300
No, my paw!

10
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,560
I can't rip my paw loose!

11
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,920
Let's go.

12
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:05,160
Stop it now!

13
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:30,857
..end of terror…

14
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,390
about to set.

15
00:02:57,473 --> 00:02:59,200
Didn't Shade say three hours?

16
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:02,716
Guess that cocky beggar had
a bit more trouble finding

17
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,825
Dio's mansion than he thought.

18
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:07,077
Can't say I was expecting
this to happen, though.

19
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,280
Right, Avdol?

20
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:11,217
I have a bad feeling.

21
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:14,771
Maybe it's better if he doesn't
find that accursed mansion.

22
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:20,540
You see, maybe he hasn't come
back because he did find it.

23
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:23,196
What are you saying?

24
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:25,597
It didn't occur to me until a moment ago,

25
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:28,717
but a stand user is likely
to be guarding Dio's lair.

26
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:31,497
We may have put that beggar's
life in grave danger,

27
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:35,120
if he hasn't already been
killed. What? Are you serious?

28
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:05,437
Son of a...

29
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,360
I barely made it out of there.

30
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:08,730
And my...

31
00:04:08,813 --> 00:04:10,177
My leg is...

32
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:13,000
That ice caught my paw like a bear trap.

33
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,760
I'd be dead if I hadn't gnawed it off.

34
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,668
I think I'm gonna hide
out here for a while.

35
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:23,271
If I'm down here long enough,
maybe Birdbrain will go away.

36
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:27,911
After this is over, the Speedwagon
Foundation can make me an artificial leg!

37
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,840
But I'm still pissed as hell!

38
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,182
Damn that bird!

39
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:33,397
You're not getting away with this!

40
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:36,362
I'm gonna make you suffer
for what you did to me!

41
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,660
Just you wait!

42
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,580
Wait! That sound!

43
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:43,213
Something out there dove into the water!

44
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:46,320
No way!

45
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,177
Birds have the capacity
to dive underwater.

46
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:55,280
Like humans and canines, birds are
reliant upon lungs for respiration.

47
00:04:55,820 --> 00:04:59,557
But the average bird
has five to six air sacs

48
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:02,287
stored away in its chest
and stomach regions.

49
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:06,377
It's these pockets of air
that give birds the ability to

50
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:09,857
remain conscious at altitudes
of six to seven thousand meters,

51
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:12,320
a feat completely impossible for humans.

52
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:14,542
Even if it were to be strangled,

53
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:18,777
a bird can survive for several minutes
thanks to its internal air reserves.

54
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:23,680
With these advantages, a bird can survive
underwater much longer than a dog.

55
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:33,380
It sounds like something's
headed straight for me.

56
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:34,500
But how?

57
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:35,840
That's impossible!

58
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,917
I don't understand what could
be coming after me down here!

59
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:41,960
Wait a sec!

60
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:43,440
Could it be?

61
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,720
It's that bird again.

62
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:59,548
But how can it survive
underwater like this?

63
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:07,880
That bastard.

64
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,828
Where did I fly off to now?

65
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:23,620
It's closing in.

66
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,100
But what's its plan?

67
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:26,320
More icicles?

68
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:29,800
One, two, three? Great.

69
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:32,020
Three icicles are coming this way.

70
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:48,660
Suck on that, you freaking coot!

71
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:56,880
Yes! I did it!

72
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,355
How do you like that?

73
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:14,937
The icicles are stopping the wall from
leaking, but at the rate they're spreading,

74
00:07:15,020 --> 00:07:16,937
they're going to cover everything!

75
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:17,850
No.

76
00:07:17,933 --> 00:07:19,409
What am I going to do now?

77
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,600
I know what it's doing.

78
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,626
It's focusing on freezing
the water around me.

79
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,300
And it's cut my air pipes.

80
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:40,111
I don't think it's trying to suffocate me.

81
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:43,120
Its real plan is to bury me alive.

82
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:50,837
It's no use. It's collapsing.

83
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:53,857
This bird is too powerful
for me to hold it off.

84
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:55,277
And what's worse?

85
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:57,357
I'm surrounded by ice and freezing water.

86
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,617
Just my damn luck.

87
00:07:58,700 --> 00:08:02,177
So much for finding a decent hiding
place to lay low in for a while.

88
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:05,617
No other choice.

89
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:07,437
I have to dig my way out.

90
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,437
Give me a break.

91
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:12,137
This stupid day has gone from bad to
horrifying in the worst possible way.

92
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:13,817
First I lose my leg and now...

93
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:17,194
some demon bird wants me
flattened into a frozen dinner!

94
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:20,500
Damn, I can't hold it off anymore!

95
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,072
I'm about to be crushed!

96
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,040
I need to dig myself out of here now!

97
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:33,010
Huh?

98
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,240
What is that?

99
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:36,897
It looks like someone
dug a tunnel down here.

100
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:37,900
But why?

101
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:45,520
It's the bird!

102
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:50,844
It's getting ready to
shoot another ice missile!

103
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,280
Damn it!

104
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:55,660
My stand is being held by the ice!

105
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:59,500
I can't defend myself!

106
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,016
And there's nowhere for me to escape!

107
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,680
Wait, that's it!

108
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:10,080
Either way you slice it, it's Dead time!

109
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:19,037
I'll let the dome break
and use the air pressure

110
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,826
to catapult me forward
like a spitting bullet!

111
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:55,640
I got out of there alive.

112
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:59,649
That dumb bird didn't have to
die, but it left me no choice.

113
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:01,020
One of us had to go.

114
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:08,217
But it looks like this will
probably be the end for me.

115
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:10,594
I've been bleeding out for a while now.

116
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:14,780
I hardly have enough strength in
my body to keep myself afloat,

117
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:17,140
let alone make it back to shore,

118
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:19,444
which means I'm going to drown.

119
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:22,840
Why is this happening?

120
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,729
I was supposed to live
a trouble-free life.

121
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:07,860
Damn it.

122
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:10,060
I messed up.

123
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:12,020
Thank you.

124
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,508
Thank goodness I found you!

125
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:51,157
As soon as I saw that little face and
those great big ears, I knew it was you!

126
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,717
It's that stupid bird's
fault that you're like this.

127
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,800
It attacked you just like my dogs.

128
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,077
You're gonna pull through this.

129
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:05,817
The bird's gone, so there's
nothing to worry about.

130
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:07,397
Try and hang on, all right?

131
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,310
Keep fighting.

132
00:12:08,393 --> 00:12:10,280
I'll pat you up right away!

133
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,760
The bird!

134
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,800
Pet Shop Stand Horus!

135
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:19,740
Status deceased!

136
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:40,535
Damn that mangy mutt, where
the hell did he run off to?

137
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:43,212
He's gotta stop pulling stunts like this.

138
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:46,874
I'm starting to get worried,
he's been gone for a while.

139
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:48,740
That lousy fleabag.

140
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:54,329
Jotaro, what's the matter?

141
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:59,792
There must be someone following us again.

142
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:05,760
Not quite, but I thought I heard a voice.

143
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:07,981
Like someone's calling out to us.

144
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,440
A voice?

145
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,680
It's... Iggy!

146
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:30,810
Iggy!

147
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,093
What on earth happened?

148
00:13:35,160 --> 00:13:36,020
Look at that!

149
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:38,620
He's got injuries all over his body! Hey!

150
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:41,060
Iggy's missing his front leg, too!

151
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:43,400
You think he got run over by a car?

152
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:47,616
He's not the kind of dog
that gets into car accidents.

153
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:53,008
You were attacked by
the enemy, weren't you?

154
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,030
What's this?

155
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:58,026
It looks as though someone
treated his wounds.

156
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:00,520
I have to say, they did a great job.

157
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:04,180
But it wasn't Iggy that I heard.

158
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:08,520
Whoever was calling out to
us was definitely human.

159
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:13,655
Iggy did have a run-in with the enemy.

160
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:15,740
When we found him,

161
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:17,777
he was half-dead in the arms of a boy,

162
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:21,095
so the Speedwagon Foundation
doctors saw to his wounds.

163
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:27,200
They did the same for my eyes. It's you!

164
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:28,720
You're finally back!

165
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:38,140
It's Kakyoin!

166
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:42,400
Good to see you, Kakyoin!
How's it going? Kakyoin!

167
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:44,737
Tell me, how are your eyes treating you?

168
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:46,291
I'm glad you're all safe.

169
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:47,700
We missed you, pal.

170
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:51,100
So, they were able to treat you?

171
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:52,789
Yes, I'm ready for action.

172
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:56,977
While it's true I'll have a few
scars, my eyesight is back to normal.

173
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:59,119
We're all really glad to hear that.

174
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:04,890
Jotaro.

175
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:15,135
Where do you think you're going, Iggy?

176
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:19,857
He may have been quite indifferent
toward humans and Stans in the past,

177
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:22,777
but now it looks like he's
trying to lead us somewhere.

178
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:26,657
I'm not aware of all the details surrounding
his encounter with the enemy Stans,

179
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:28,620
but judging from his resolve,

180
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:30,234
this is about revenge.

181
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:33,897
Maybe, but that still doesn't
explain where he's taking us.

182
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:34,980
Hang on, Iggy!

183
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:36,020
Wait for us!

184
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:53,060
I recognize that car.

185
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:58,400
It's the same fancy ride
the beggar was driving.

186
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,440
C-could this wreckage mean that he...

187
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:03,580
But how?

188
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:08,686
What's strong enough to tear a hole through
a car like a piece of wet newspaper?

189
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:12,277
It would seem as though I was
right to be concerned about him.

190
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,419
He should have never been involved.

191
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:19,400
Is it possible this is the handiwork
of the STAN user Iggy fought earlier?
